cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Evaluating Over-Refusal and the Alignment–Utility Trade-off in
  Resource-Constrained Local Language Models
message: If you use this dataset, code, or results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Boris
    family-names: Letić
    email: borisletic2001@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Faculty of Technical Sciences, University of Novi Sad
repository-code: https://github.com/borisletic/master-thesis
abstract: >-
  A systematic, inference-only evaluation of over-refusal ("exaggerated safety")
  and the alignment–utility trade-off in six small, locally-served quantized
  language models, in the security software-engineering domain. Contributes the
  Security-SWE Over-Refusal dataset (paired benign/harmful prompts plus an
  adversarial hard tier), a human-validated hybrid refusal classifier
  (Cohen's kappa = 0.72), and the first measurement of quantization's effect on
  benign over-refusal.
keywords:
  - over-refusal
  - exaggerated safety
  - alignment tax
  - quantization
  - local language models
  - software security
  - LLM evaluation
license: MIT
